The robotic arm is powered by a 2S 7.4V LiPo battery. Power passes through an XT60 connector, inline fuse, and main power switch before reaching the Waveshare ESP32 servo controller. The controller sends commands to the servos over a shared bus, allowing each servo to move independently while using the same communication line. The larger ST3215 servos handle the main arm joints, while the smaller SC15 and SC09 servos control the wrist, claw rotation, and claw movement. A voltage regulator is used for the smaller servos so they receive the correct voltage.
